{"id":"rs_tmp_goqmpqwh8x","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I'm weighing whether the vault write counts as a working-tree write under plan mode's restrictions — since the vault lives outside the repo but the write is still a state-changing action, it may still fall under the plan mode guard that blocks anything beyond local session artifacts.

Given that ambiguity, I think the safe path is to avoid actually writing either the repo file or the vault note, and instead search the vault read-only and check the repo for the existing ProjectRecord decision to ground a draft, then present the drafted text to the user rather than committing it.

